Upstream PR:     apache/superset#39835 "feat: Allow specific mcp tools to be
                 disabled", commit 70419e9d8f81477026eba57fb1fc32e7abbc0e65,
                 merged 2026-05-18.
Affects:         Apache Superset 6.1.0 (this commit landed 17 days after the
                 6.1.0 tag, 2026-05-01 — not present in the version this
                 charm tracks).

What it adds: MCP_DISABLED_TOOLS, a Flask-config set of exact tool names.
  init_fastmcp_server() removes each one from the live FastMCP instance at
  startup via mcp.local_provider.remove_tool(name) (unknown names log a
  warning, not an error) before generating the server's instructions text.
  get_default_instructions() also gained a disabled_tools parameter that
  strips any instruction line mentioning a disabled tool, so the LLM is
  never told to call a tool it can't reach. This is the mechanism intended
  for suppressing a built-in tool superseded by a custom extension tool of
  the same purpose.

